    "result_text": "The full test suite passes: **271 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the membership number feature so that each newly created owner receives a sequential membership number equal to one more than the current number of owners, returned in the owner response as the integer field `membershipNumber`.\n\nChanges:\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `membershipNumber` integer (`int32`) property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field. The MapStruct `OwnerMapper` auto-maps it (name matches the entity property), so no mapper change was needed.\n- **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a persisted `membershipNumber` field (`membership_number` column) with getter/setter, mirroring the existing `registrationDate` field.\n- **`controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 In `addOwner`, after the duplicate checks pass and before saving, set `owner.setMembershipNumber(findAllOwners().size() + 1)`.\n- **Schema files** (h2, hsqldb, mysql, postgres) \u2014 Added the nullable `membership_number INTEGER` column to the `owners` table.\n\nThe JDBC repository's `SimpleJdbcInsert` auto-detects the new column from table metadata, and JPA maps it via the entity annotation, so persistence works across all repository profiles. Existing seeded owners keep a null membership number, which is fine since the spec only concerns newly created owners.",
